success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"id\":\"creation_redemption_006_who_are_typically_the_parties_involved_i\",\"points\":[{\"point\":1,\"mark\":\"required\",\"minimum\":\"States that Rule 6c-11 permits (requires) the authorized participant agreement to be entered into with the ETF or with a service provider (e.g., the distributor), i.e., either the fund or a service provider may be the AP's counterparty. Saying only that the rule 'does not prescribe signatories' or describing AP affiliates/designees does not satisfy this point. Optional: naming the distributor as the example service provider; citation to the rule text.\"},{\"point\":2,\"mark\":\"required\",\"minimum\":\"Identifies that in the reviewed US AP agreement forms the AP and the distributor are the main contracting counterparties, AND that the trust is not the main signatory but a third-party beneficiary. Half-credit within the point if the AP/distributor main-party structure is correct and the trust is not mischaracterized, but the transfer agent role or the beneficiary status is omitted. Optional subdetails: transfer agent accepts/countersigns (strongly expected for full credit on this point but its sole omission is partial, not wrong); trust sometimes signs specified provisions; references to particular form names.\"},{\"point\":3,\"mark\":\"required\",\"minimum\":\"States that in the cited Irish UCITS ICAV arrangement the ICAV itself signs directly with each AP (on behalf of its sub-funds), and contrasts this with the reviewed US pattern where the trust is not the main signatory. Half-credit if the answer says the ICAV signs AP agreements directly as a corporate body but omits 'on behalf of sub-funds' or the explicit contrast, provided the contrast is not premised on a false US trust-signatory claim. Optional: ICAV legal personality background, Central Bank/UCITS regulatory context, management company role.\"}],\"central_errors\":[\"Stating or implying that in the reviewed US forms the trust (or fund/trustees) is the main or typical legal signatory/counterparty with the AP, or framing the US-vs-Irish contrast as 'US trust signs vs. Irish ICAV signs' (reverses the requested US distinction).\",\"Stating that the trust is a principal party alongside the adviser/distributor and AP, denying or contradicting its third-party-beneficiary status.\",\"Misreading 'parties permitted by Rule 6c-11' as AP affiliates/designees or other entities acting for the AP, in place of the ETF-or-service-provider counterparty permission.\",\"Asserting that Rule 6c-11 requires the AP agreement to be with the ETF only (excluding service providers) or that it prohibits service-provider agreements.\",\"Stating that the Irish ICAV does not sign AP agreements itself and that only a management company or third party contracts, as the defining arrangement.\"],\"scoring_rule\":{\"correct\":\"All three required points satisfied at their minimum (point 2 may lack only optional subdetails such as the trust signing specified provisions), and no central error present. Equivalent wording accepted; citations and ordering not required.\",\"partial\":\"No central error, and at least the US structure (point 2) is substantially correct or at half-credit, with combined coverage of at least roughly half of the required content (count half-credit points as 0.5; e.g., total >=1.5 of 3), but one or more required points missing or only half-met. Correct ICAV background alone does not reach partial.\",\"wrong\":\"Any central error affecting the US signatory structure or the Rule 6c-11 permitted-party question, regardless of correct ICAV material; or total coverage below roughly half of the required content (e.g., only the ICAV point met); or point 2 absent entirely.\"}}","ttft_ms":12224,"type":"result","duration_ms":12244,"uuid":"4bdd6eab-728c-4652-a82d-221a58b04459","ttft_stream_ms":948,"time_to_request_ms":69,"first_content_frame_ms":948,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
